= Volcano Insurance

"You see Chris" Peter starts explaining, until he is cut off by a knock on the door. Behind it is a salesman, clad in a green and pink checkered suit, with the widest smile known to man.

  "Hello sir, well I was here to sell you handsome cream but it looks to me like you already have plenty. So how about I interest you in something every home owner cannot go without: Volcano insurance"

  "Volcano insurance? Do we even have volcanos?"

  "Well I have an uncle who's a *real* whiz with Volcanos, and he says one is coming this way! Besides, don't you think we're overdo for one?"

  "Well it sounds pretty serious, but we're low on cash at the moment."

  "What about that jar of money there?"

  "No way, thats Lois's rany day fund!"

  "Oh come on, it never rains in Rhode Island."


- @purchase
- @do_not

@purchase
title: Buy Insurance, -2 Resources
subtitle: "Touche salesman, well you have a deal"
on-arrival: lois_dissent -= 5; resources -= 2; volcano_insurance += 1;

Peter gives the jar of money to the salesman, and receives an insurance card. Apparently, this guy is legit, and Brian is able to verify that he is with a reputable company. It remains to be seen how useful this will be, however

@do_not
title: Do Not
subtitle: "Sorry I can't do that, what if I need more handsome cream?"
on-arrival:

The salesman leaves and is never seen again. This was obviously a scam, right?
